This agreement is between you and the maker of PlainVoice ("we"). By installing or using
PlainVoice (the app, its engine, the `plainvoice` command, its MCP server and its Claude Code
plugin, together "the Software") you accept it. If you do not accept it, do not install or use
the Software.

1. Licence to use

   We grant you a non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to install and use the Software on
   computers you own or control, for personal and commercial purposes. The Software is licensed,
   not sold. We keep all rights not expressly granted here.

2. Free and Studio

   The Software's Free features need no licence key. The Studio features (the Chatterbox voices
   and voice cloning) need a valid licence key, which is the key of a PlainTake licence bought
   through Gumroad. A Studio licence is perpetual: it does not expire and needs no renewal. It is
   for the person or organisation that bought it, and you may activate it on the computers you
   use. Do not publish or share your key. A refunded, charged-back or disputed purchase does not
   grant a licence.

3. Your output

   The audio, captions and timing files you make with the Software are yours, and you may use
   them for any lawful purpose, including commercially, without royalties to us. You are
   responsible for the text you voice and for how you use the output. You must have the rights to
   that text. You may clone a voice only with the speaker's permission, from a clip that is
   theirs, and you must not use the output to impersonate or deceive anyone. Every audio export
   carries a metadata marker saying it is AI-generated speech.

4. Restrictions

   You may not:
   (a) copy, sell, rent, lend, sublicense or redistribute the Software, or offer it as a hosted
       service to others;
   (b) reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the Software, except as far as the law
       applicable to you allows it despite this restriction;
   (c) remove or bypass the licence check, or remove the notices in the Software;
   (d) use the Software in breach of the law.

5. Third-party components and models

   The Software uses third-party software and model weights, which are listed in NOTICE.md. Each
   is licensed to you under its own licence, which governs it and is not limited by this
   agreement. Model packs are downloaded from their publishers or from our release channel when
   you ask for them.

6. Network use

   The Software connects to the network only when you ask it to: to download a model pack, to
   activate a licence key with Gumroad, and to check for updates. It sends no telemetry.

7. No warranty

   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING
